>>
endobj
202 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (     As a team associated with an online school, our members are geographically dispersed across multiple time zones but concentrated in Northern California. Even within NorCal, some members must drive as much as 1.5 hours to attend in-person meetings. Consequently, we meet in an onsite-offsite model, which allows members to contribute remotely.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (      On Friday afternoons, we meet on Adobe Connect, a teleconferencing platform. During this short meeting, we handle higher-level tasks, such as outlining prototype concepts, distributing tasks, or developing our game strategy. The online format ensures that all members can be involved in important decisions. On Saturdays, we meet for 5-6 hours in-person at a site in the Bay Area. There, on-site members prototype, assemble, and test the robot, while offsite members can call in to work on software and design. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
