328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (     Whether it be linear discriminant analysis or the Gram-Schmidt process, our STEM Course Series shares knowledge on a broad variety of STEM topics, like linear algebra. With many members of  our team taking university-level courses, we aim to decrease the barrier for high school students to access such resources. Rather than explaining topics in dense technical terms, we brought in real-world motivations to make engagement accessible.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (     We invited multiple speakers to our school, ranging from individuals in academia to industry. We started by bringing our past vice captain, Thomas Lu, a current physics and computer science student at Berkeley. Thomas shared the lessons he learned in participating through FTC and its impact, not only in college, but in his identity. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (      In addition, we invited Cole Johnson, an alumnus of our school. He is both a researcher and entrepreneur from Georgia Tech and Caltech. From Cole, the team learned a lot about the applications of robotics in other fields of study. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
